   01274| // Drop a trailing follow-up instruction clause ("… and summarize who won",
   01275| // "… . Compare their patents") from a query. A universal boundary algorithm, not
   01276| // a list of memorised fragments: a follow-up clause is one of the lexicon's
   01277| // followup_instruction_verb surfaces sitting immediately after a *boundary* —
   01278| // sentence punctuation or a run of clause_continuation_marker words — and the
   01279| // query is cut at the start of the earliest such boundary. A bare verb with no
   01280| // boundary before it is part of the topic and left untouched. Mirrors
   01281| // truncate_search_instruction_tail in src/solver_handlers/web_search_intent.rs.
   01282| // Issue #1175 R3, numeric group: claim evidence joined into claimEvidence() (formal_ai_worker_dispatch.js), each the operand reader its handler already runs, twin of rust/src/capability_routing/claims.rs.
